ike trail it passes underneath  an interstate highway and it leads you  to a walmart  but you can you can take a bicycle there  and ride the rails where buster filmed  just very briefly uh the scene where  he's kicked out of line  the barn in the background was on  south river road on the east side of  town  and then  when the heroes returned from home  that house is still standing on adams  and 16th street  now they did have to travel a little bit  so for the conclusion of the film  when they crashed the bridge  they filmed it near culp creek and that  was about 15 miles away from town and by  the way dorina lake  several of the the intermediate train  stations where scenes were filmed were  filmed along the rail line and they're  covered up now by dorina lake so i don't  have any photos of them but  but anyway the the conclusion of the  film was filmed  by cult  and  the  the train lay fixed in the riverbed for  years until it was finally pulled out  for world war ii for scrap so there  really isn't much of the film of the  train left  but that uh that concludes my little  comments about the general  you
 

